<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 12-MAR.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 12-MAR.</headline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Justin, with 50 mph winds, is in the Coral Sea near 16.3s/151.5e, and nearly stationary. Little change in strength or little movement is expected during the next 48 hours...although a slow westward drift is possible. Justin will threaten shipping through the period as seas in the region will continue quite rough.  </p>
<p>There are no further emergency statements at this time.</p>
</text>
